nodes.title:
Teardown lane retell (account-free), after the adversarial verifier: 67 graded claims (50 observed, 10 inferred, 5 vendor-claimed, 2 unknown) and 12 pre-registered account-phase predictions with falsifiability notes. The verifier confirmed 23, corrected 14, downgraded 4, added 7 and left 19 out-of-scope claims unchecked. Sources:
- docs llms.txt (356 pages) and llms-full.txt (338 pages split);
- the OpenAPI (109 ops, 319 schemas, revision 2026-10-19);
- pricing (re-fetched 19:27Z, unchanged), changelog, status API (50 incidents) and the Ashby job board;
- DNS/RDAP, AWS IP ranges and a client-subnet DNS re-run;
- the web SDK source via npm pack (not installed);
- a slimmed HAR of the dashboard login redirect;
- REA web-bundle analysis of the pricing page;
- 19 India-relevant community threads read in full.
Neither the lane nor the verifier could write report.md or verify.md (the harness refuses .md report files from subagents); the report and verification text are in the workflow's structured output, and the per-claim verification record is in claims.json (verification, claim_lane, grade_lane fields) and predictions.json (verifier_check).

Retell account-phase questions (after the verifier):
- dashboard surface and the Campaigns screen (retries, pacing, DNC settings);
- KYC path for team@ (a Persona ID of a real person; one ID verifies one account, so this is the owner's call);
- whether Indian card or UPI payment works;
- time from dashboard login to first call on an Indian handset via a Retell US number vs a BYO Plivo or Vobiz trunk (sign-up itself was already done by Instinct, ~10 min);
- handset reply gap on Indian PSTN (predicted p50 1.6-2.4 s) with the SDP media address from each call's PCAP (LiveKit Indian /24 or US block);
- messy-CSV behaviour on batch calls (opt-out row predicted to be dialled);
- the scope of the 4,000-token billing rule;
- voicemail detection on Indian operator messages;
- whether an API-created agent with no handbook_config still says it is an AI when asked;
- whether a 1600-series line can be trunked to Retell's US SIP edge at all.
